<li>
<p>developed by Jack Volder in 1959</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>developed as an iterative algorithm to convert between polar and cartesi=
an coordinates using ONLY shift, add, and subtract operations</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Has two modes of operation (circular rotation and vectoring) that can be=
 used to support computation of trig,hyperbolic, linear and logarithmic fun=
