<h2 class=3D"mume-header" id=3D"speed-and-pipelining">Speed and Pipelining<=
/h2>

<ul>
<li>CORDIC requires n+1 iterations
<ul>
<li>
<p>single hardware iteration stage</p>
<ul>
<li>if run at system clock, computation suffers latency and low throughput<=
/li>
<li>if using run at a fast clock, multi-clock-domain design must be introdu=
ced</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>
<p>pipelining allows throughput to "match" system clock rate (still have la=
tency)</p>
<ul>
<li>requires hardware per iteration, typically more area</li>
<li>stages are simplified as they are specialized for each iteration. LUT f=
or the allowed <span class=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><math xml=
